    <statement><p>Values of <m>f(x,y)</m> are given in the table below.  Let <m>R</m> be the rectangle <m>1 \leq x \leq 1.6, 2 \leq y \leq 3.2</m>. Find a Riemann sum which is a reasonable estimate for <m>\int_R f(x,y) \, da</m> with <m>\Delta x = 0.2</m> and <m>\Delta y = 0.4</m>.  Note that the values given in the table correspond to midpoints.</p>
<p><me>\begin{array}{|c || c|c|c|}
\hline
y \backslash x \amp  1.1 \amp  1.3 \amp  1.5 \\ \hline \hline
2.2 \amp  -3 \amp  8 \amp  -3 \\ \hline
2.6 \amp  6 \amp  -1 \amp  10 \\ \hline
3.0 \amp  2 \amp  2 \amp  7 \\ \hline
\end{array}</me></p>
<p><m>\int_R f(x,y) \, da \approx</m> <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2.24</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
